            'Quotient rule: $Z_x=\\dfrac{(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)-\\frac{x+y}{2\\sqrt x}}{(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2}$, so '
            '$xZ_x=\\dfrac{x\\sqrt x+2x\\sqrt y-y\\sqrt x}{2(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2}$.',
            'By symmetry $yZ_y=\\dfrac{y\\sqrt y+2y\\sqrt x-x\\sqrt y}{2(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2}$.',
            'Add: numerator $x\\sqrt x+x\\sqrt y+y\\sqrt x+y\\sqrt y=(x+y)(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)$, so the sum is '
