MNEMONICS = ['<i>“Subscripts walk forward, partials walk back.”</i> $z_{xy}$: $x$ then $y$; $\\frac{\\partial^2z}{\\partial '
 'y\\,\\partial x}$: read from the right, $x$ then $y$.',
 '<i>“Fix the other, slope the trace.”</i> To read $f_x$ at a point, fix $y$, look at the trace, and take its slope.',
 '<i>“Multiply down, add across.”</i> In a tree diagram, multiply the derivatives along each path from the top to the '
 'variable you want, then add the paths.',
 '<i>“Implicit: minus, top over the one you want.”</i> $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=-\\dfrac{f_x}{f_y}$: the variable you '
 'differentiate by ($x$) on top, the one you solve for ($y$) below.',
 '<i>“Order k brings the falling product.”</i> First order $n$, second $n(n-1)$, third $n(n-1)(n-2)$; the coefficients '
 'follow the binomial row 1, 2, 1 or 1, 3, 3, 1.',
 '<i>“Undo, test, divide.”</i> Undo the outer function to get $f(u)$, test $f(u)$ for its degree $n$, then divide: '
 "$g=n\\,f/f'$.",
 '<i>“Binomial brackets.”</i> Order $n$ is $\\frac1{n!}(h\\partial_x+k\\partial_y)^nf$: coefficients 1, 2, 1 at second '
 'order and 1, 3, 3, 1 at third.',
 '<i>“Series, table, values, substitute, check.”</i> The five steps of every class 008 problem (Figure F33.1).',
 '<i>“Determinant first, then $r$.”</i> Positive Hessian: $r$ negative = hill (max), $r$ positive = valley (min); '
 'negative Hessian = saddle; zero = doubt.',
 '<i>“Case, point, table, value.”</i> Split the factored equation into cases, collect the points, tabulate $r$ and '
 '$rt-s^2$, then substitute for the values.',
 '<i>“Add, differentiate, divide out $\\lambda$, constrain.”</i> $F=f+\\lambda\\phi$; $F_x=F_y=F_z=0$; equate the '
 'expressions for $\\lambda$; finish with $\\phi=0$.']
